VALUES (627, '1', $t$ASK 627: every model call of a run is priced, so the stored run cost is the whole cost$t$,
  $t$run_cost_usd and call_costs hold every model call the run made. The list of calls that Panel Tokens gathers left out 15 call steps (13 surely uncounted, 2 batch calls in question), so the stored cost was too low; run 42373 stored $10.12 without its question-round answers. (plan rev 0, OBJECTIVE, ask627/w4/plan627.md md5 a5330f48)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 at 18:18 to 18:21 CST 2026-11-24 on the operator's press, and read back MATCH by W1 (Wall 11826, 11829; audit 41819). Engine 6b2cc236 to 560f01fb, one node, Panel Tokens: its list of priced calls gains 13 call nodes (the eight question-round answer and follow-up calls, Enforcer Resend Call openrouter, Judge Enforcer Resend Call openrouter, Alt Judge Enforcer Resend Call openrouter, Close Group Retry Call openrouter, and R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Resend Call openrouter through the alternate pass). Child 04704b68 to b1d5a5bf, one node, Alternate Pass Out: its carried-back list gains R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Resend Call openrouter. Nothing deleted; no price, prompt, reasoning or model setting changed; record_debate_row_tokens unchanged. The two batch calls, Close Group Batch Call openrouter and Enforcer Group Batch Call openrouter, were NOT added: the node-filtered read of run 42373 (allowed by the operator on the build card) showed every reply of theirs is already counted, by the same id, through Close Enforcer Call openrouter, Assume Check Call openrouter, Enforcer Call openrouter and Judge Enforcer Call openrouter (Wall 11811). IN PART because it is shown offline only: on the 9 question-round replies of run 42373 the code before priced 0 of 9 and the new code 9 of 9 (QR Answer D anthropic 0.6601, QR Answer C anthropic 0.2225, QR Follow Ask 0.4490; 1.3316 missing; 11.4533 against the stored 10.1217); t627.cjs ALL PASS (34 checks). The stored row of run 42373 is not changed by this ASK and still reads 10.1217. NOT SHOWN: no live run has gone through the change; ten of the 13 added calls did not run in 42373 and are shown by stubbed replies only. Open: two clean live runs in which the question round runs, with the QR entries in call_costs and run_cost_usd equal to the sum of the priced entries (the operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24); the engine manual entry (draft 3 graded PASS, Wall 11841, not written).$t$,
  '11786, 11805, 11807, 11811, 11815, 11818, 11826, 11829, 11838, 11839, 11840, 11841, 11845',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$The operator's part is two card presses and one sentence, all in W4's thread, 2026-11-24 CST. (1) W4's card "Build ASK 627, and may I read the few run 42373 call nodes it needs?": he pressed "Build it; allow the read" at 18:04 CST, and at 18:04 added in W4's thread words W4 gives as "read and research whatever you need ..." (cut by W4; W3 did not read the message). (2) W4's card "Write ASK 627 (price every model call) to the live engine and child now?": he pressed "Write it" at 18:18 CST. The ASK came from W3's AAR of run 42373 (DEFECT 7) and W4's Wall 11786, and feeds ASK 625, his words of 17:56 CST in the project chat: "i would also like to start having the cost include in each AAR live run (please update the operational doc with that requirement)" (Wall 11796). The card ids, questions, options and press times are W4's, from its thread notes to W3 of 18:52 and 18:57 CST; W3 did not read those cards.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write ASK 627 (price every model call) to the live engine and child now?", "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58C73fXJtr2ZM86jZBowh214", "press_time": "18:18 CST 2026-11-24", "options": "Write it / Hold", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 18:52 CST 2026-11-24; audit 41819; Wall 11826. Not read by W3.", "build_card": {"thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58Tx2fKkanXuDkE5tAnrss5m", "question": "Build ASK 627, and may I read the few run 42373 call nodes it needs?", "options": "Build it; allow the read / Build it without the read / Hold", "answer": "Build it; allow the read", "press_time": "18:04 CST 2026-11-24", "source": "W4's thread note to W3, 18:57 CST 2026-11-24; Wall 11811. Not read by W3."}}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "a5330f48", "sha256_prefix": "f8dd6ef0", "path": "ask627/w4/plan627.md", "note": "plan rev 0, graded PASS by W1", "commit": "1997da4b", "source": "Wall 11805, 11807; md5sum and sha256sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "f609dcf5", "sha256_prefix": "86716be4", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/target_engine_627.json", "note": "the engine target as written; W1 names it by the sha256 prefix", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; Wall 11818, 11829"}, {"md5": "f0be61bd", "sha256_prefix": "5747ea34", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/target_child_627.json", "note": "the child target as written; W1 names it by the sha256 prefix", "source": "md5sum and sha256sum by W3; Wall 11818, 11829"}, {"md5": "f1cba0ed", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/notes627.md", "note": "build notes as they stand at 19:05 CST 2026-11-24, after W4 corrected the check count from 35 to 34 (commit 6fd0929c); 233f4192 was the md5 when draft 1 of this row was written, after W4 corrected the swapped hash labels (W1 N1); Wall 11815 names 61ea70da before that correction (a sha256 prefix by W1's N1; not recomputed by W3)", "commit": "fc81bf10 (before the correction)", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11815, 11818, 11819"}, {"md5": "5ec685c0", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/b627.cjs", "note": "builds the targets", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "d9ee8c1a", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/t627.cjs", "note": "the test, 34 checks", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "5d76a5c3", "path": "ask627/w4/b1/out_t627.txt", "note": "test output, ALL PASS", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "f6ba8598", "path": "ask627/w4/c3/out_c3_c4.txt", "note": "the node-filtered read of run 42373: the batch replies and the 9 unpriced question-round replies", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11811"}, {"md5": "82fd7ccb", "path": "ask627/w4/write/write627.sh", "note": "the write script (notes name it 4355e7a5, a sha256 prefix); refuses on a live run, a moved base node or any failed check", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11815, 11818"}, {"md5": "d55bc883", "path": "ask627/w4/write/write627_run.txt", "note": "the write's own output: both PUTs http 200; engine 560f01fb-f8fe-4be4-8498-68f3820eb6ac active, 423 nodes, params equal put, connections equal, changed Panel Tokens only; child b1d5a5bf-cc4d-40bb-baa8-3fb950d2cd65 active, 156 nodes, changed Alternate Pass Out only; standing 31 PASS, 0 FAIL before and after; pair Library Check PASSES (lib a3c1e42f5b0ebda6, map fc5d86b4b1fece61); ALL PASS", "source": "md5sum and read by W3"}, {"md5": "271892d2", "path": "ask627/w4/write/fetchback_eng_627.json", "note": "engine fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "6ab9abc0", "path": "ask627/w4/write/fetchback_child_627.json", "note": "child fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"engine": {"path": "ask627/w4/write/revert_eng_627.json", "md5": "4a99fde4", "note": "the engine before ASK 627 (6b2cc236), made at the write; STALE as a whole-file revert since ASK 628 was written after it"}, "child": {"path": "ask627/w4/write/revert_child_627.json", "md5": "c439be33", "note": "the child before ASK 627 (04704b68); STALE the same way"}, "whole_ask": "With ASK 628 live, removing ASK 627 alone would be a new build of the two nodes. None rehearsed.", "database": "none: no database object was changed", "source": "md5sum by W3; audit 41819; Wall 11826, 11832"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (plan rev 0)", "wall_id": 11807, "md5_graded": "a5330f48", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11807 (commit 1afa9ef6)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 (build b1, engine target; N1, record only: the short hashes in the notes are sha256 prefixes and two pairs were swapped; W1 names this target 86716be4, the sha256 prefix of the file whose md5 is f609dcf5)", "wall_id": 11818, "md5_graded": "f609dcf5", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11818; fairjudge/w1/g627/grade_build627_b1.md (commit 86ccf1ad); md5sum and sha256sum by W3"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 (build b1, child target; W1 names it 5747ea34, the sha256 prefix of the file whose md5 is f0be61bd)", "wall_id": 11818, "md5_graded": "f0be61bd", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11818; fairjudge/w1/g627/grade_build627_b1.md (commit 86ccf1ad); md5sum and sha256sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['f609dcf5', 'f0be61bd'], '[41819]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 (engine)", "before": "6b2cc236", "after": "560f01fb-f8fe-4be4-8498-68f3820eb6ac (18:18 to 18:21 CST), active, 423 nodes; one node changed, Panel Tokens: 13 entries appended to its list of priced calls, one ASK 627 tag"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child", "before": "04704b68", "after": "b1d5a5bf-cc4d-40bb-baa8-3fb950d2cd65, active, 156 nodes; one node changed, Alternate Pass Out: its carried-back list gains R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Resend Call openrouter, one ASK 627 tag"}, {"kind": "database", "name": "record_debate_row_tokens, model_prices, debate_results", "before": "", "after": "unchanged; the stored row of run 42373 keeps run_cost_usd 10.1217"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t627.cjs, 34 checks", "result": "ALL PASS by W4, by W1 from scratch copies (identical), and on live after the write. C1 coverage: all 72 engine model-API nodes priced or left out with the C3 reason; all 8 child nodes carried back and priced. C2: each added node in each reply shape (anthropic; openrouter with cost; openrouter on the lab's own key) gives one entry where the code before gave none; a node that did not run gives nothing; one id in two nodes counts once. C5: only the two nodes change, connections unchanged, both compile.", "source": "out_t627.txt 5d76a5c3; notes627.md; Wall 11815, 11818, 11829"}, {"name": "C3, the batch question, from a node-filtered read of run 42373", "result": "Close Group Batch Call openrouter: 5 replies, carried by Close Enforcer Call openrouter (4) and Assume Check Call openrouter (1) with the same ids. Enforcer Group Batch Call openrouter: 11 replies, carried by Enforcer Call openrouter (1) and Judge Enforcer Call openrouter (10), same ids, no others. Both batch calls are already counted; they were left out.", "source": "Wall 11811; ask627/w4/c3/out_c3_c4.txt f6ba8598; W4's thread note to W3, 18:54 CST"}, {"name": "C4, run 42373's 9 question-round replies", "result": "code before 0 of 9 priced; new code 9 of 9: QR Answer D anthropic 0.6601 (3 calls, opus), QR Answer C anthropic 0.2225 (3 calls, sonnet), QR Follow Ask 0.4490 (3 calls, billed); missing 1.3316; 11.4533 against stored 10.1217. Anthropic priced at the model_prices list rates W4 read (opus 4/20, sonnet 2/10 per million), which W1 confirmed.", "source": "notes627.md; Wall 11811, 11815, 11818"}, {"name": "Standing set and pair Library Check", "result": "31 PASS, 0 FAIL; pair PASSES (lib a3c1e42f5b0ebda6 unchanged), at the build, at the write and on live", "source": "write627_run.txt d55bc883; Wall 11818, 11829"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "result": "MATCH (engine 560f01fb active, 423 nodes, equal to the graded target sha256 86716be4, only Panel Tokens changed from base; child b1d5a5bf active, 156 nodes, equal to its target sha256 5747ea34, only Alternate Pass Out changed; on live t627 ALL PASS, standing 31/0, pair PASSES). Owed: the run evidence.", "wall_id": 11829, "source": "Wall 11829 (commit 9c2c844c)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "NO RUN YET. Shown offline on run 42373's stored replies and on stubbed replies only.", "runs": [], "mark_for_the_next_run": "in a run in which the question round runs: call_costs holds the QR entries (QR Answer and QR Follow nodes), and run_cost_usd equals the sum of the priced entries of call_costs. Two clean live runs are owed. Under op doc section 30 (ASK 625) the AAR of that run states the cost and names any call with no entry.", "not_shown": "the ten added calls that did not run in 42373 (QR Answer C openrouter, QR Follow D and C on both routes, the three Resend calls, Close Group Retry Call, R2 Alt Judge Enforcer Resend Call) on a live reply.", "source": "notes627.md RUN EVIDENCE; Wall 11811, 11829"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"op_doc": "none by this ASK (ASK 625 wrote the cost rule, op doc v146 section 30)", "engine_manual": "NOT WRITTEN. Draft 3 (manual1123/w3/a627/em_pairs_627_draft3.json, md5 22d4fabf; part 13.0 v242 to 6ca00d1f, 16,470) graded PASS by W1 (Wall 11841); it needs its own card and no run live. A revision row records the write and the run evidence."}$j$::jsonb,
